PDE-a   words=20 verbatim=True :: The parent-death signal is sent upon subsequent termination of the parent thread and also upon termination of each subreaper process
PDE-b   words=12 verbatim=True :: The parent-death signal setting is cleared for the child of a fork(2).
PDE-c   words= 7 verbatim=True :: The parent-death signal is process-directed (see signal(7))
CM-a    words=17 verbatim=True :: A fenced code block begins with a code fence, preceded by up to three spaces of indentation.
CM-b    words=15 verbatim=True :: The content of a code fence is treated as literal text, not parsed as inlines.
CM-c    words=13 verbatim=True :: The closing code fence must use the same character as the opening fence:
CM-d    words=14 verbatim=True :: The closing code fence must be at least as long as the opening fence:
CM-e    words=17 verbatim=True :: A code fence is a sequence of at least three consecutive backtick characters (`) or tildes (~).
